00:29:59.839 --> 00:30:08.070
<v Yusra Haddad>He does. He asked for the new go-live date for the minutes this morning, before the alarm.

00:30:09.532 --> 00:30:13.945
<v Folasade Renwick>Ramona, anything from the programme side before I decide?

00:30:14.881 --> 00:30:30.813
<v Ramona Szabo>Only that the faculty already think of it as Yusra's. When people email me about Tinderbox, they cc Yusra, not Mara. So whatever you decide, the faculty won't be surprised.

00:30:32.444 --> 00:30:34.208
<v Folasade Renwick>Good to know.

00:30:39.731 --> 00:30:42.031
<v Folasade Renwick>Okay. I've heard enough.

00:30:42.881 --> 00:30:52.916
<v Folasade Renwick>Here's what I'm deciding. Yusra owns Tinderbox from today. Mara stays architect of record and hands over the runbooks.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:31:04.610
<v Folasade Renwick>Bart, that's Kestrow running it. Through Yusra's team, on Kettleyard. The platform stays central. The service is yours.

00:31:05.881 --> 00:31:11.625
<v Bart Ngata>I can live with that. It's most of what I asked for.

00:31:12.260 --> 00:31:20.467
<v Folasade Renwick>It's the part of what you asked for that I can give you this month.

00:31:22.105 --> 00:31:24.431
<v Yusra Haddad>Okay. I'll take it.

00:31:25.550 --> 00:31:41.297
<v Mara Ilves>So architect of record means: the tenant, the gateway contract and the interface spec still come through me. Day-to-day decisions on the pilot - courses, onboarding, the standup, the go-live call - are Yusra's.

00:31:42.019 --> 00:31:55.277
<v Folasade Renwick>That's right. And if the two of you ever disagree on something that touches the platform, it comes to me. Not to the Council, and not to Bart's office.

00:31:56.168 --> 00:31:57.428
<v Bart Ngata>(laughs) Noted.

00:31:58.595 --> 00:31:59.646
<v Yusra Haddad>Understood.

00:32:01.138 --> 00:32:07.521
<v Ramona Szabo>So for the dashboard: owner Yusra, Mara as architect of record. Got it.

00:32:08.686 --> 00:32:19.526
<v Folasade Renwick>And Hyun-woo's review doesn't move. He reviews the package Mara sent him, whoever owns the pilot. Nobody goes around him.

00:32:20.182 --> 00:32:21.504
<v Yusra Haddad>Nobody would.

00:32:22.544 --> 00:32:27.666
<v Bart Ngata>I've had that conversation with Hugo once before. Once was enough.

00:32:29.364 --> 00:32:37.430
<v Yusra Haddad>And Mara, you're still on the standup invite. I'm not letting you off that easily.

00:32:39.183 --> 00:32:40.426
<v Mara Ilves>(laughs) Fair.

00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:51.204
<v Bart Ngata>My deans will be pleased. They've been asking me for a month who they're supposed to complain to.

00:32:52.737 --> 00:32:55.474
<v Folasade Renwick>Now they know. It's Yusra.

00:32:56.765 --> 00:32:59.298
<v Yusra Haddad>Thank you, Sade. Very kind.

00:33:00.520 --> 00:33:01.508
<v Ramona Szabo>(laughs)

00:33:02.663 --> 00:33:18.508
<v Bart Ngata>I'll say this, Sade, since we're being candid. This is the first time in a while the System has handed Kestrow something instead of the other way round. People will notice that.

00:33:19.713 --> 00:33:36.741
<v Folasade Renwick>That's deliberate. Kettleyard only works if campuses want to be on it. If every campus feels like a tenant in somebody else's building, they'll build their own. Which is your argument, I know.

00:33:38.215 --> 00:33:45.230
<v Bart Ngata>It's my argument. I'm glad it's been heard, even if it's been heard and declined.

00:33:47.096 --> 00:33:53.070
<v Folasade Renwick>Heard, and partly answered. The service is yours. The platform isn't. Not now.

00:33:54.507 --> 00:34:10.319
<v Mara Ilves>And for what it's worth, the architecture doesn't care who owns the service. The spec, the tenant, the gateway - none of that changes because Yusra's name is on it instead of mine.

00:34:11.996 --> 00:34:14.874
<v Bart Ngata>Good. Then nothing breaks on Monday.

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:19.096
<v Mara Ilves>Nothing breaks on Monday.

00:34:21.216 --> 00:34:44.372
<v Bart Ngata>Which brings me back to money. If it's ours from today, who pays for the spring term? Because I'll be honest, I don't have a line for it. I didn't budget for a service I didn't own, and I can't find one in March.

00:34:46.217 --> 00:34:50.620
<v Folasade Renwick>I know. I've been thinking about this since Tuesday.

00:34:52.502 --> 00:34:57.692
<v Ramona Szabo>Do you want us to drop off for this bit?

00:34:58.805 --> 00:35:02.270
<v Folasade Renwick>No. Stay. You'll all need to know.

00:35:08.746 --> 00:35:09.679
<v Folasade Renwick>Okay.

00:35:10.925 --> 00:35:20.196
<v Folasade Renwick>And Kestrow's spring term won't be charged back - central covers it. We'll centrally fund the spring term at Kestrow.

00:35:22.155 --> 00:35:34.577
<v Folasade Renwick>Expansion beyond Kestrow is still conditional on chargeback. That doesn't change. Saltmarren, Orrin Valley, Brackwater - if they want a Tinderbox, they sign up to chargeback first.

00:35:36.237 --> 00:35:39.999
<v Mara Ilves>So that's a partial reversal of Tuesday.

00:35:41.264 --> 00:35:56.361
<v Folasade Renwick>Partial. I'm taking Kestrow's spring term out of the condition. That's the only thing I'm taking out. Kestrow's pilot was never the point of that rule; the other three campuses were.

00:35:58.647 --> 00:36:02.780
<v Bart Ngata>Thank you. That helps a great deal. Genuinely.

00:36:04.046 --> 00:36:07.095
<v Ramona Szabo>And after the spring term?

00:36:08.157 --> 00:36:14.765
<v Folasade Renwick>After the spring term, Kestrow is a Council question like everything else.

00:36:15.593 --> 00:36:20.126
<v Bart Ngata>Fine. I'll take spring and argue about autumn.

00:36:22.264 --> 00:36:25.117
<v Folasade Renwick>(laughs) I'm sure you will.

00:36:26.014 --> 00:36:35.972
<v Ramona Szabo>Can I check what 'covers it' covers? Is that just the platform share, or the model usage as well?

00:36:36.877 --> 00:36:48.282
<v Folasade Renwick>All of it, for Kestrow's tenant, for the spring term. I'm not going to split hairs over one term of one pilot.

00:36:50.153 --> 00:36:53.513
<v Mara Ilves>Percy's going to have a view.

00:36:54.885 --> 00:36:59.901
<v Folasade Renwick>Percy always has a view. It's still my decision.

00:37:01.021 --> 00:37:07.661
<v Bart Ngata>Can I say that to my deans? That the spring term is covered?

00:37:08.566 --> 00:37:13.307
<v Folasade Renwick>You can say it. Out loud. No numbers.

00:37:14.502 --> 00:37:20.523
<v Bart Ngata>No numbers. Understood. They won't ask for numbers, they'll just be relieved.

00:37:22.805 --> 00:37:27.199
<v Yusra Haddad>Mara, practically. What am I inheriting? What actually moves?

00:37:28.556 --> 00:37:44.554
<v Mara Ilves>The tenant runbook, the gateway escalation path, the on-call contacts at Kettleyard, the deployment checklist, and the dummy-data procedure until Hyun-woo clears real data. I'll hand over the operational runbooks to you.

00:37:46.148 --> 00:37:50.978
<v Yusra Haddad>Good. And Greta's tier-1 runbook slots in under those?

00:37:51.950 --> 00:38:05.014
<v Mara Ilves>It sits in front of them. Greta's is what the desk does on the first call. Mine is what happens after the desk escalates. They should reference each other.

00:38:07.303 --> 00:38:17.123
<v Yusra Haddad>And who's on call for the platform side? If it's two in the morning and the gateway's down again.

00:38:19.018 --> 00:38:25.334
<v Mara Ilves>The gateway on-call is Bartosz on Ilya's team. Bart from platform.

00:38:27.320 --> 00:38:29.693
<v Bart Ngata>Not me, I hope.

00:38:30.376 --> 00:38:33.599
<v Mara Ilves>(laughs) Not you. The other Bart.

00:38:35.162 --> 00:38:38.984
<v Yusra Haddad>Two Barts. Wonderful. I'll put surnames in everything.

00:38:40.242 --> 00:38:46.964
<v Ramona Szabo>We've been doing that in the dashboard since Monday. It saves a lot of confusion.

00:38:47.841 --> 00:38:51.049
<v Yusra Haddad>Okay. Let's take the details offline.

00:38:53.047 --> 00:38:54.352
<v Mara Ilves>Offline, yes.

00:38:55.406 --> 00:38:56.365
<v Folasade Renwick>Bart?

00:38:58.106 --> 00:39:22.596
<v Bart Ngata>Then send me the cost model. If Kestrow's going to be in the model after spring, I want to see what the model says about Kestrow before I walk into the Council. I don't want to see my campus's number for the first time on a slide.

00:39:24.837 --> 00:39:39.814
<v Folasade Renwick>Here's my problem, Bart. I've said that nothing on the chargeback options goes to the campuses in writing before the Council. Not the paper, not the tables, not a summary in an email.

00:39:40.998 --> 00:39:44.447
<v Bart Ngata>I'm not the campuses. I'm one campus.

00:39:45.779 --> 00:39:49.001
<v Folasade Renwick>(laughs) You're exactly the campuses.

00:39:49.876 --> 00:39:54.785
<v Bart Ngata>And I'm the one you just gave a service to.

00:39:58.760 --> 00:40:09.419
<v Folasade Renwick>Fair. Okay. Ramona, send Bart the Kestrow tab of the chargeback cost model only - that's the one exception to nothing-in-writing.

00:40:11.125 --> 00:40:16.367
<v Ramona Szabo>I'll send it to you, Bart. Just the Kestrow tab.

00:40:17.467 --> 00:40:25.633
<v Folasade Renwick>Just the Kestrow tab. Not the other campuses, not the options paper. And Bart, please don't forward it.

00:40:26.731 --> 00:40:29.169
<v Bart Ngata>Understood. It stays with me.

00:40:29.840 --> 00:40:45.743
<v Bart Ngata>I want to be able to say to my deans, hand on heart, that I've seen what the model says about us. That's all. I'm not going to wave it around at the Council.

00:40:46.968 --> 00:40:52.676
<v Folasade Renwick>I believe you. That's why it's one tab and not the paper.

00:40:53.588 --> 00:41:01.449
<v Ramona Szabo>Bart, I'll send it to you directly, not to your office inbox. Is that alright?

00:41:02.084 --> 00:41:05.048
<v Bart Ngata>Directly is better. Thank you, Ramona.

00:41:06.716 --> 00:41:17.489
<v Bart Ngata>Mara, one more. Could you at least cost an internal build? Just so I've got a number to hold up against that tab.

00:41:18.589 --> 00:41:20.714
<v Mara Ilves>If Sade wants it.

00:41:22.479 --> 00:41:26.411
<v Folasade Renwick>Not now, Bart. Let's get through go-live first.

00:41:28.010 --> 00:41:30.438
<v Bart Ngata>Fine. I'll keep asking.

00:41:32.114 --> 00:41:34.519
<v Folasade Renwick>I know you will.

00:41:36.440 --> 00:41:43.929
<v Bart Ngata>I've been asking the System for things for eleven years. Persistence is most of the job.

00:41:45.811 --> 00:41:49.266
<v Folasade Renwick>(laughs) It's most of mine as well.

00:41:50.676 --> 00:42:00.836
<v Yusra Haddad>For what it's worth, Bart, I'd rather not build a gateway either. I have enough to do in April.

00:42:02.267 --> 00:42:03.701
<v Bart Ngata>(laughs) Traitor.

00:42:05.903 --> 00:42:06.703
<v Yusra Haddad>Pragmatist.

00:42:07.646 --> 00:42:24.333
<v Ramona Szabo>Can I pick up one more thing while we're on money? On Tuesday I said 'we'll loop in the campus CFOs', and then nobody actually owned it. I'll take the campus CFO briefing - verbally.

00:42:26.506 --> 00:42:28.831
<v Folasade Renwick>Verbally. Before the Council.

00:42:31.088 --> 00:42:37.769
<v Ramona Szabo>Verbally, before the Council. Phone calls. No slides, nothing in an email.

00:42:39.286 --> 00:42:42.380
<v Mara Ilves>Thank you. That one was hanging.

00:42:44.667 --> 00:42:49.076
<v Folasade Renwick>Conversations, Ramona. Not decks. Not 'just a quick summary'.

00:42:51.063 --> 00:42:55.563
<v Ramona Szabo>Conversations. I promise. The slides stay at home.

00:42:57.100 --> 00:43:03.091
<v Folasade Renwick>Good. Because when I say 'not in writing', I mean not in writing.

00:43:03.738 --> 00:43:07.666
<v Ramona Szabo>I know. I was there on Tuesday.

00:43:09.863 --> 00:43:17.927
<v Mara Ilves>Mona, while you're at it - can you hold Thursday the 11th for Council prep with Sade?

00:43:19.762 --> 00:43:25.508
<v Ramona Szabo>On it. I'll get a prep slot from Lulu for Thursday.

00:43:26.039 --> 00:43:29.441
<v Folasade Renwick>Thursday's fine. Morning if you can.

00:43:30.641 --> 00:43:42.969
<v Folasade Renwick>Good. From here the chargeback model is in Council prep. No new options, no new tabs except Bart's. Mara, the one-pager still comes to me Wednesday.

00:43:43.949 --> 00:43:44.749
<v Mara Ilves>Wednesday.

00:43:45.326 --> 00:43:48.309
<v Folasade Renwick>Anything else before we stop? Bart?

00:43:49.894 --> 00:43:54.048
<v Bart Ngata>No. That's more than I came in with.

00:43:55.793 --> 00:43:56.740
<v Folasade Renwick>Yusra?

00:43:59.034 --> 00:44:03.089
<v Yusra Haddad>No. I'm going to go and find Greta.

00:44:04.375 --> 00:44:06.329
<v Mara Ilves>Nothing from me.

00:44:07.777 --> 00:44:10.726
<v Ramona Szabo>Nope. I've got my list.

00:44:11.331 --> 00:44:15.035
<v Folasade Renwick>Thank you, all. Yusra, congratulations, I think.

00:44:16.616 --> 00:44:19.172
<v Yusra Haddad>(laughs) Thank you. I think.

00:44:19.802 --> 00:44:23.248
<v Folasade Renwick>Bart, go and get some sleep.

00:44:24.467 --> 00:44:29.624
<v Bart Ngata>After my two o'clock. Thank you, Sade. Thanks, everyone.

00:44:30.557 --> 00:44:31.896
<v Ramona Szabo>Bye, all!

00:44:32.525 --> 00:44:33.978
<v Mara Ilves>Thanks. Bye.
